# python / validators
tests/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# os
.DS_Store

# local secrets (none expected in core, but never commit one)
.env
.env.*

# `cafe dev` GENERATES this from cafaye.yml and rewrites it on every run — the
# file says so in its own first line ("Do not edit: every run rewrites this
# file"). It is build output shaped like a source file, which is why it needs
# saying here rather than relying on it being untracked by accident: an
# untracked generated file is one `git add -A` away from being committed, and
# from there it is a merge conflict nobody can resolve by reading it.
#
# THIS ONE WAS COMMITTED, once. `8007d07` ("core: record kit-32's second
# non-database image reference in the fleet scan") swept it in beside a real
# change to tests/test_specs.py, and nothing about that commit made the file look
# deliberate — which is the argument above, demonstrated rather than asserted.
# Nothing in this repository reads it: no test, no workflow, no document and no
# source file has ever named `caf.dev.compose.yaml`, so removing it from the
# index loses no reference. core holds no docker-compose.yml, so there is no
# hand-written counterpart here to confuse it with.
/caf.dev.compose.yaml
keyring/
secrets/
